From: f <f@f>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: iris: Raise MXC to the corner the core needs

The iris OPP table of SM8450 gives the MXC rail SVS at 366 MHz and
SVS_L1 at 444 MHz (measured on hardware: the first required-opp lands
on MXC, the second on MMCX). The downstream videocc driver of the same
platform requires SVS_L1 up to a 1098 MHz and NOMINAL up to a 1332 MHz
video_cc_mvs0_clk_src, i.e. for the 366 and 444 MHz core rates, on
both MXC and MMCX (videocc-waipio.c rate_max of video_cc_mvs0_clk_src).

With MXC one corner low the video core runs out of spec at its two
top rates. Decoding happened to survive it; starting an encode session
takes the 444 MHz point and reset the whole SoC the moment the
firmware touched the VPP.

Raise the first required-opp of both points: SVS_L1 at 366 MHz and
NOMINAL at 444 MHz, matching the downstream requirement.

Local Diting bring-up change, not submitted upstream.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
@@ -3322,13 +3322,13 @@
 
 				opp-366000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <366000000>;
-					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_svs>,
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_svs_l1>,
 							<&rpmhpd_opp_svs_l1>;
 				};
 
 				opp-444000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <444000000>;
-					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_svs_l1>,
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>,
 							<&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
 				};
 			};
